kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "package-tui-editor-autocomplete"
purpose: "TBD - created by archiving change c430-port-editor-autocomplete. Update purpose after archive."
valid_scope[2]: src/,tests/
requirements[4]{req_id,title,statement}:
  ea01,"autocomplete-provider-integration","The Editor MUST support an optional AutocompleteProvider set via set_autocomplete_provider(). The provider MUST be invoked on Tab keypress (explicit), on / at line-start (slash-command auto-trigger), and on trigger characters (@ and custom) at token boundaries. When the provider is None, Tab/newline/Enter MUST fall through to normal editor behavior."
  ea02,"autocomplete-selectlist-popup","When autocomplete returns suggestions, the Editor MUST create a SelectList popup with the suggestions, compute a best-match pre-selection (exact value match > prefix start match), and render it below the editor border in render(). While the popup is active, Tab/Enter MUST apply the selected item via provider.applyCompletion(), Esc MUST cancel the popup, and up/down arrows MUST navigate the list. After applying, the popup MUST close and the cursor MUST be positioned to the post-completion location."
  ea03,"edit-cursor-refresh","After any text insertion (insertCharacter), deletion (handleBackspace/handleForwardDelete), or cursor movement (moveCursor/wordLeft/wordRight), if autocomplete is active the Editor MUST call update_autocomplete() to refresh the suggestion list so it stays in sync with the text before the cursor. For single-result Tab-completion (force+explicitTab), the result MUST auto-apply without showing the popup."
  ea04,"request-serialisation-and-debounce","Multiple rapid autocomplete requests MUST be serialised by an autocomplete_start_token counter; only the latest request applies its results. For @-attachment triggers, a 20ms debounce delay MUST be enforced. For explicit Tab or force-file completions, the debounce delay MUST be 0. The editor MUST NOT block the main thread during autocomplete; async execution MUST use an optional tokio Handle, falling back to sync when absent."
scenarios[5]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  ea01,"slash-trigger-on-tab",editor cursor is at the start of a line after typing /hel and a provider is set,Tab is pressed,the provider's get_suggestions is called and a SelectList appears below the editor
  ea02,"selectlist-enter-applies","autocomplete popup is showing with first item pre-selected",Enter is pressed,the item's value replaces the prefix at the cursor position and the popup closes
  ea02,"selectlist-esc-cancels",autocomplete popup is showing,Escape is pressed,the popup closes without modifying the text
  ea03,"backspace-updates-suggestions",autocomplete is showing suggestions,backspace removes a character from the prefix,update_autocomplete is called and the suggestion list changes to match the new prefix
  ea04,"rapid-tabs-drop-stale",three Tab presses arrive in quick succession,only the final one's suggestions apply,the first two are discarded because the start_token increments
